window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-030", "name_zh": "活力", "name_en": "Vitality", "tagline": "活力在赛斯那里不是「精力旺盛」，而是宇宙的基本材料：你的身体、一块石头、一个念头，都是同一种生命力换的装——而且它永远用不完，因为每用一次就多生出一些。", "explanation": "活力在赛斯语料里有两层意思，而且第一层常常被忽略：它首先不是「精力好」，而是宇宙的基本材料——内在生命力。万物都是它的「伪装」：肉体、岩石、飞碟、原子和分子，全是这股生命力换的装；它填满所有形式，自己却无形，一丁点儿就能播种一整个宇宙，而且它自行增生——每表达一次，就多出新的活力，所以行动永远完不成自己，循环永不结束。落到个人身上，活力是流经你的东西：自我若不接纳它，它就压抑或爆炸；身体有自己充满活力的身体意识，能自动修正不平衡，疗愈的底牌就是「物质由赋予它生机的内在特质形成」。把活力找回来的路子都很日常：暗示对准健康而非症状、多而短的睡眠、自发性、游戏般的 Work、不被信念干预的生物乐观。往大处看，它是群体事件、战争与主义背后的能量账本。赛斯自己就是最好的示范——一个按人间说法「已经死了」的人格，比教室里的活人更有生命力：他关心的从来不是你早餐吃了什么，而是你整体的灵性活力。", "definitions": [{"zh": "行动不是外在对物质起作用的一股力量。反之，行动是内在宇宙的内在生命力。它是介于内在生命力想要完全让自己物质化的欲望动力，以及它没法这么做的无能为力之间的两难困境。", "en": "Action is not a force outside that acts upon matter. Action is, instead, the inside vitality of the inner universe. It is the dilemma between inner vitality's desire and impetus to completely materialize itself, and its inability to completely do so.", "source": "Session 138"}, {"zh": "真正的空间，第五维度空间，就是所有存在本身的生命力和原料，充满活力且生气盎然。", "en": "Instead true space, fifth dimensional space, is the vitality and stuff of all existence itself, vital and alive.", "source": "Session 43"}, {"zh": "它们全都是由内在生命力形成的，而内在生命力就是基本或基础实相。", "en": "They are all formed from inner vitality, which is the basic or ground reality.", "source": "Session 305"}, {"zh": "你的身体有一个充满了能量与活力的整体身体意识，它自动地改正任何的不平衡。", "en": "Your body has an overall body consciousness filled with energy and vitality. It automatically rights any imbalances.", "source": "Session 624"}, {"zh": "你在这里不是为了替人类的苦痛号哭，而是当你发现不喜欢它们时，透过你内心的喜悦、力量和活力来改变它们。", "en": "You are not here to cry about the miseries of the human condition, but to change them when you find them not to your liking through the joy, strength and vitality that is within you.", "source": "Session 615"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "活力是什么：宇宙的最底料", "note": "AI总结：在赛斯的早期课里，「生命力」是他给出的第一个宇宙论答案：万物的积木由同样的元素组成，元素不断改变位置，把内在生命力或燃料从一种伪装转化成另一种。肉体是一个在更大伪装模式里运行的伪装模式，但它同时也是宇宙重要内在原料的转换器，让生命力能在各种新条件下运作。所以别因为看不见就否认它——就像没人因为看不见空气而否认空气。真正的空间不是待填充的空无，第五维度空间就是所有存在本身的生命力和原料，充满活力且生气盎然；这股生命力构成一切伪装，它是最直接、最亲密的那一面，却比伪装多得多，而且它充满所有其他形式，自己却是无形的。到《灵魂永生》里他说得更直接：岩石、山岳与大地是活的伪装；而所有层面与系统都由内在生命力形成——那就是基本或基础的实相。判断：活力不是生命的属性，是先于一切「东西」的那个东西。", "src": "第 16、19、20、23、43、133、135、305、522 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 16 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 19 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 20 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 23 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 43 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 133 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 135 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 305 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 522 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0007", "zh": "细小金属线内的层面，也就是，由我们想像的金属线连结和交互连结形成的层面，进入每个不同层面的领域之中，呈现出那个层面本有的形式。所以，如果我们小小打个比喻，这些金属线会变粗、变细，或完全改变颜色，像某只变色龙之类的动物，呈现每个邻近森林地盘物质化的外在，持续不停伪装它真实的外表。所以，任何一个层面的居民，也都像变色龙，都像动物，固化活力金属线看起来并不像分界或间隔，它们看起来和那个层面物质化的其他东西完全是同一类。", "en": "The planes within the tiny wires, that is the planes formed by the connections and interconnections of our imaginary wires, come into the sphere of each different plane and take on the form inherent in the plane itself. Therefore these wires, if we may use a small analogy, will grow thick or thin, or change color completely, like some chameleon-like animal constantly camouflaging its true appearance by taking on the outward manifestations of each neighboring forest territory. Then too, the inhabitants of any particular plane are chameleon like, animal like. Solidified vitality wires do not look like boundaries or divisions. They appear exactly of the same type as the other materializations on that particular plane.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第16节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "16", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0014", "zh": "飞碟的现形，来自科学技术比你们地球进步得多的一全层面。但是，这仍然不是一个心智科学层面。所以，这套多少看得见的伪装行头一出现，你们才会这么惊讶。现在，生命力从一个表面形式转换为另一种形式的趋势是如此强烈，因此你们看到的飞碟，其实不是属于你们的层面，也不是属于它本来层面的东西了。这种情况是怎么回事呢？事实是：当飞碟，就用你们喜欢的所谓的称呼吧，开始飞向目的地的时候，结构上组成它的原子和分子——原子和分子本身则是由生命力形成的——或多或少是按照它自己的领域加诸其上的模式排列的。现在，随着这个东西进入你们的层面，扭曲就发生了。飞碟的实质结构陷入了形态的两难之局，陷入了要么完全把自己变成地球的特殊伪装模式，要么保留其原有模式的两难之中。地球上的观察者根据他对宇宙极少的认知，企图把他看到的和他大概知道或想像有可能的东西关联在了一起。", "en": "The flying saucer appearances come from a plane that is much more advanced in technological sciences than earth at this time. However this is still not a mental science plane. Therefore the camouflage paraphernalia appears, more or less visible, to your own astonishment. Now, so strong is this tendency for vitality to change from one apparent form to another, that what you have here in your flying saucers is something that is actually, as you view it, not of your plane nor of the plane of its origin. What happens is this. When the flying saucer as you prefer to call it starts out toward its destination, the atoms and molecules that structurally compose it, and which are themselves formed by vitality, are more or less aligned according to the pattern inflicted upon it in its own territory. Now as this enters your plane a distortion occurs. The actual structure of the craft is caught in a dilemma of form. It is caught between transforming itself completely into earth’s particular camouflage pattern, and retaining its original pattern. The earthly viewer attempts to correlate what he sees with what he supposedly knows or imagines possible, in the little he knows of the universe.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第16节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "16", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0021", "zh": "我这里在空气之外又加上了水，然而，它们还是由同样的元素组成。这些元素，就是建构我们伪装的积木。即便在你们层面，空气和水也有多种形式。这些元素不断地改变位置，把内在生命力或燃料，从一种伪装转化成另一种。那么为什么当这件事以不同的伪装顺序发生在其他层面时，会这么难以理解呢？", "en": "I have added here the addition of water to air, yet they are composed of the same elements. The elements are the blocks which build our camouflage. Air and water have many forms even on your plane. The elements change position constantly to transform the inner vitality or fuel from one camouflage pattern to another. Then why is it so difficult to understand that this happens on other planes and under different camouflage sequences?", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第19节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "19", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0027", "zh": "肉体是一个在更大的伪装模式里运行的伪装模式。但是，肉体以及所有伪装模式，从另一个方面来讲，也是宇宙的重要内在原料转换器，因此这个生命力能够在各种各样新的条件下运作。", "en": "The physical body is a camouflage pattern operating in a larger camouflage pattern. But the physical body and all camouflage patterns, looked at in another manner, are also transformers of the vital inner stuff of the universe, where this vitality is then enabled to operate under new and various conditions.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0034", "zh": "沿着这些思路我想说另一个重点。我敢肯定没有人会因为在日常生活中看不见空气就否认它的存在。没有人会因为不了解自己的肺是用什么方法呼吸，而否认空气的存在。他们知道他们在呼吸，也知道没有呼吸，难免会死。否认空气的存在是很荒谬的，只因为这种生命力通常不可见，或因为你不了解自己怎么使用它，就否认它的存在，也一样荒谬。", "en": "Now I wish to make another point along these lines. No one, I am sure, denies the existence of air because ordinarily you do not see it. No one denies the existence of air because they do not understand the method by which their own lungs breathe. Yet they know that they breathe, and they know that without breath death is inevitable. To deny the existence of air would seem ridiculous. It is just as ridiculous to deny this vitality because it is usually unseen, or because you do not understand how you use it.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0061", "zh": "你们只所以认为空间是一个有待于填充的空无，是因为在你们的层面上，你们用伪装模式填充你们所说的空间。我再说一次：反之，真正的空间，第五维度空间，就是所有存在本身的生命力和原料，充满活力且生气盎然，所有其他的存在透过我目前为止相当概略勾勒的方法，从中交织。即使在你们的层面，质（quality）代表一种扩展，但它不一定意味着空间的扩展。宇宙以一种质的方式持续扩展，与一般想像的空间无关。而这种扩展比我这时候能够向你们做的解释更加生动又有效。", "en": "You think of space as an emptiness to be filled because on your plane you fill what you call space with camouflage patterns. And I repeat: instead true space, fifth dimensional space, is the vitality and stuff of all existence itself, vital and alive, from which all other existences are woven through means which I have outlined so far in a rather sketchy fashion. Even on your plane quality, which represents a kind of expansion, does not necessarily imply an expansion of space. The universe expands continually in a qualitative manner that has nothing to do with space as it is usually envisioned. And the expansion is more vivid and valid than I can possibly explain to you at this time.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0085", "zh": "所以不应该把存有想成是圆满（completed）的。你们所知极少的电子宇宙是一个实相，但它也是另一个实相的象征。因为甚至在这个电子宇宙背后，都有一个就语言来说无法探索的实相；因为所有的意识，虽然都有一个电子实相，但甚至在这之外还有一个实相。 电子实相的成因就是这个宇宙以及所有宇宙的生命力，而构成一切万有的宇宙生命力，是无法触及的。它就是碰触，但不是你们以为的碰触。这个生命力就是在所在场域之内构成伪装外观那个最立即和亲密的面向。可是它显然比伪装还多。", "en": "The entity should therefore not be thought of as completed. The electric universe, of which you know so little, is a reality, and yet it is also a symbol of another reality. For behind even this electrical universe there is a reality which cannot be explored in terms of speech; for all consciousness, while having an electric reality, has a reality beyond even this. It is the vitality of the universe, and all universes, which causes the electrical reality, and the vitality of the universe, composing everything that is, cannot be touched. It is touch, but touch not as it is conceived of in your terms. This vitality is the most immediate and intimate aspect that composes the camouflage appearance within all fields. And yet it is by far more than the camouflage.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第133节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "133", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0089", "zh": "对你们来说，很难思考那独立于它自身物质化之外的存在。这种生命力充满其他所有的形式，同时它自己，用你们的话来说，却是没有形式的。但我们针对电子宇宙的讨论应该已经带领你们进入无形界域之中。", "en": "It is most difficult for you to contemplate the existence of that which is independent of its own materialization. This vitality fills all other forms while it is itself, in your terms, formless. But our discussions concerning the electrical universe should have led you into intangibles.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第135节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "135", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0142", "zh": "其他层面和系统与你们自己的层面和系统一样真实，也一样不真实。它们全都是由内在生命力形成的，而内在生命力就是基本或基础实相。很多其他的系统更加清楚反映内在实相，有着更少的扭曲，但扭曲本身就是创造。所有的系统于是在心智里形成，包括你们自己的系统。", "en": "Now, other planes and systems are as real and as unreal as your own. They are all formed from inner vitality, which is the basic or ground reality. Many other systems reflect inner reality more clearly, with less distortions, but the distortions themselves are creations. All systems are then formed mentally, including your own.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第305节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "305", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0239", "zh": "你的物质环境里的背景，有时很可爱的那些行头设备，你所知的生活的物质面，全都是伪装，因此我叫你的物质实相为一种伪装。这些伪装却是由宇宙的活力所组成的。岩石、石头、山岳与大地是活的伪装，由你无法知觉的微细意识形成互相连锁的心灵之网。在其内的原子与分子有它们自己的意识，就如你体内的原子分子也一样。", "en": "The settings in your physical environment, the sometimes lovely paraphernalia, the physical aspects of life as you know it, are all camouflages, and so I call your physical reality a camouflage. Yet these camouflages are composed of the vitality of the universe. The rocks and stones and mountains and earth are living camouflage, interlocking psychic webs formed by minute consciousnesses that you cannot perceive as such. The atoms and molecules within them have their own consciousness, as do the atoms and molecules with your body.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第522节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "522", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "它怎么变成东西：行动、伪装与原子", "note": "AI总结：活力变成万物不是自动的、也不是无意识的——那个面向内在实相世界的自己，相当有意识地汲取本有的生命力与素材来建构物质；但如果你不理会内在感官的资料，就会和伪装模式缠得太深，只能汲取到非常有限的额度。在潜意识之内有一种机制，允许意念或内在生命力物质化为物理建构——这能力连原子和分子都有。最关键的一步是「行动」：行动不是外在对物质起作用的一股力量，而是内在宇宙的内在生命力——是内在生命力想完全物质化的冲动，与它做不到这件事之间的两难。正因为这个两难，行动基本不可能完成它自己：内在生命力不管以任何形式物质化，马上就倍增进一步物质化的可能性，而它是自行增生的，一丁点儿就能播种一整个宇宙。落到物理层面，想法和情绪以自身的电磁实相，形成有活力的物理产物，叫做原子和分子。判断：世界不是被「造」出来的，是活力在永远完不成的表达里持续冒出来的。", "src": "第 31、34、51、55、137、138、139、144、463 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 31 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 34 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 137 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 138 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 139 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 144 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 463 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0047", "zh": "为了物质建构的目的，原始生命力会实际汇聚在一起，然而这过程并不是真的自动化，也不是真的无意识地进行。我讲过强大的自我意识自己、你自己人格没有觉察到的自我意识自己，这个面向内在实相世界的自己，相当有意识地汲取本有的生命力与素材。", "en": "This actual gathering up of prime vitality for the purpose of physical construction is not however truly automatic, and it is not truly performed unconsciously. The strong self-conscious self of which I have spoken, the self-conscious self of which your own personality is not aware, this self that faces into the inner world of reality, quite consciously draws upon the vitality and stuff of what is.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0054", "zh": "不理会内在感官的资料，人格就会与伪装模式深深纠缠在一起，对于提供他们基本能量与力量的生命力，能够汲取的额度非常有限。在和你们自己一样的文化导向层次里，伪装模式变得极为复杂且极具限制性，所以这种情形更常发生。", "en": "When the data from the inner senses is ignored the personalities then become so intertwined with the camouflage pattern that they are only capable of drawing upon a very limited amount of the vitality which gives them basic energy and strength. This happens more usually than not in such culturally-oriented levels as your own, where the camouflage pattern becomes extremely complicated and imprisoning.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第34节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "34", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0069", "zh": "在潜意识之内也有一种机制，允许意念或内在生命力的物质化或投射，成为物质建构。这个能力是原子、分子和更小粒子与生具有的。", "en": "There is also a mechanism within the subconscious that allows for the materialization or projection of idea or inner vitality into physical construction. This capacity is inherent even in the atom and molecule and smaller particles.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0071", "zh": "这似乎奇怪的原因是，你们没有完全理解被个人化为意识的能量、生命力，形成肉体；而且一旦它出现在你们的层面上，就能离开肉体，再自己重组起来。在某一方面来说，对它穿越而过的原子和分子，它不过就像拂过树梢的风。", "en": "This seems strange because you do not fully comprehend that the energy, the vitality that is individualized into consciousness forms the physical body; and once it appears on your plane it can leave the body and reassemble itself. It would represent no more in one way to the atoms and molecules through which it passed, than the wind that passes through the treetops.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0093", "zh": "当你读这份资料时，将会有更多你最初没发觉的东西。行动尽可能接近内在生命力或能量中，无法在任何伪装之内、在任何层面之内，完全物质化的那个部分。行动本身由于这个原因而无法被直接（划线）感知。但伪装上的效应倒是经常可以被感知。", "en": "There will be much more in this material when you read it, than you may at first realize. Action approximates as nearly as possible that portion of inner vitality or energy which cannot be completely materialized within any camouflage, within any plane. Action itself cannot be directly （underlined） perceived for this reason. But is effects upon camouflage can often be perceived.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第137节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "137", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0097", "zh": "再说一次，行动不是外在对物质起作用的一股力量。反之，行动是内在宇宙的内在生命力。它是介于内在生命力想要完全让自己物质化的欲望动力，以及它没法这么做的无能为力之间的两难困境。这在处理物质宇宙首先在物质场域出现的课里也简短讨论过。", "en": "Once more, action is not a force outside that acts upon matter. Action is, instead, the inside vitality of the inner universe. It is the dilemma between inner vitality’s desire and impetus to completely materialize itself, and its inability to completely do so. This was also discussed briefly in sessions dealing with the first appearance of matter within the physical field.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第138节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "138", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0101", "zh": "行动基本上根本不可能完成它自己。内在生命力，不管以任何形式物质化，马上就倍增进一步物质化的可能性。同时，因为内在生命力是自行增生的，所以只需要一丁点儿内在生命力就可以播种一整个宇宙。", "en": "Action basically can never complete itself. Inner vitality, materializing in any form whatsoever, at once multiplies the possibilities of further materialization. At the same time, because inner vitality is self-generating, only a minute fraction of inner vitality is needed to seed a whole universe.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第138节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "138", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0105", "zh": "首先我想要确定你们了解行动，在我们已经讨论过的范围内。行动是所有实相的内在生命力。它寻求它自己尽可能多方面得到利用。然而，它的行动，它向外物质化的企图，必定创造出新的内在生命力，因为这就是组成它的原料。而且这股新的内在生命力接着会寻求物质化，所以这个循环永远不会结束。", "en": "First I want to make certain that action is understood, insofar as we have discussed it. Action of the inner vitality of all reality. It seeks to utilize itself in as many ways as possible. Its action, its attempts at outward materialization, however, must result in the creation of new inner vitality, for this is the stuff of which it is composed. And this new inner vitality will then seek materialization, and so the cycle is never completed.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第139节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "139", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0109", "zh": "为了我们的客人好，让我说一下，行动就是宇宙的生命力，所有的实相都源自于它。这会让我们的讨论变得比较简单。再一次，没有任何行动可以被撤消。没有任何东西静止不动。因此，当我们的客人在他的两扇门中间犹豫不决时，他并非静止不动，而是在犹豫不决上使用一样多应该用在有意义方向上的能量。", "en": "For the benefit of our visitor, let me say that action is the vitality of the universe from which all realties spring. This will make our discussion simpler. Again, no action may be withdrawn. Nothing is motionless. Therefore, when our visitor hesitates between his two doors, he is not motionless, but uses as much energy in indecision as should be expended in purposeful direction.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第144节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "144", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0213", "zh": "因此在物理上，你们感知到的是一个内在事件的近似。那个内在事件从根本上不是物质的。（停顿。）现在，我尽量说得简单——想法和情绪以自身的电磁实相，形成有活力的物理产物，叫做原子和分子。这就是我在我们早期关于迷宫和电线的比喻里告诉你们的基本内容。", "en": "Physically then you perceive an approximation of an inner event. The inner event basically is not physical. (Pause.) Now, as simply as I can put this, thoughts and emotions form, of their own electromagnetic reality, vitalized physical products called atoms and molecules. This is basically what I told you in our early analogy with the mazes and the wires.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第463节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "463", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "自我与活力的拔河：为什么你感觉没电", "note": "AI总结：活力到个人这里，第一道闸门是自我。正因为内在活力没有被自我接受，它一旦被认可就显得像要爆发——自我总是不惜代价想维持稳定与耐久，回避无可避免的改变。甚至看起来像是阻碍的行动，也可能突然变成建设性的新方向，让原来的个体焕然一新、增添活力和力量。人格的基本生命力可以被统一起来——罗就有过那次「所有存在中的第一次」：理智从直觉部分学习、被释放而非被征服，整个人格的基本活力汇拢在一处。身体需要你拒绝给它的那股活力时，它会以别的形式要回来——奥古斯都的分裂正由此而来。两条硬道理：一是你现在的生活并没有贯注在你活力的全部潜能上；二是活力与生命是「赐予你、流经你」的——你可以决定拿它做什么，但它是流过你的，不完全属于你。每个读者都该以某种对自己很新的方式感觉到自己的活力，发现内在打开的扩展之路。判断：没电的感觉多半不是能量没了，是闸门关了。", "src": "第 161、163、395、405、440、558、591、633 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 161 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 163 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 395 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 405 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 440 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 558 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 591 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 633 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0116", "zh": "就是因为内在活力没有被自我接受，所以一旦受到自我认可，似乎就具有相当大的爆发力。自我试图，这个自我试图，逃避与拒绝无可避免的改变。这个个案的自我，如同其他个案一样，不惜任何代价，一心想维持住稳定性与耐久性。", "en": "It is precisely because the inner vitality is not accepted by the ego, that when it is acknowledged by the ego it seems so explosive. The ego attempts, this ego attempts, to stand aside and to deny the inevitability of change. The ego in this case, as in many cases, attempts to maintain stability and permanence at all costs.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第161节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "161", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0122", "zh": "事实上，并没有固定不变的规则可以告诉你们，哪些行动基本上来讲是阻碍性的行动，哪些不是。因为外表看来或许像是阻碍性的行动，实际上也可能突然成为一种建设性的新指引，最后也可能代表一种更新、更强大的本体模式和完整模式，而让原来的个体全然更新，并增添其活力和力量。", "en": "There is indeed no hard and fast rule to tell you which actions are basically impeding actions, and which are not. For what may appear an impeding action may indeed turn out to be the burst of a new and constructive direction, which may eventually represent a new and stronger pattern of identity and integrity, that will completely refresh the original unit and add to its vitality and strength.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第163节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "163", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0168", "zh": "理智是从自己的直觉部分学习，尚未被征服，但已经被释放。力量，也就是整个人格的基本生命力，已经汇集在一起，或者更确切地说，在这一次的存在中，第一次统一起来。（赛斯－珍指着我强调）也是所有存在中的第一次。", "en": "The intellect has learned from the intuitive portions of the self. It has not been conquered, it has been freed. The force, the basic vitality of the whole personality, has been gathered together, or rather is just being united for the first time in this existence. (Jane, as Seth, pointed at me for emphasis.) And for the first time in any existence.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第395节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "395", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0179", "zh": "他不必害怕自己自发性的自己，这个自己不会背叛他。久未消失的手臂症状代表一种压制因素，心电感应的确存在，存在的生命力远比他想象的要大得多。人真的有天生的防卫力，他不必那么（划线）密切监控自己的念头。", "en": "He need not fear his spontaneous self. It will not betray him. The arm symptoms still hanging on represent an inhibiting factor. Telepathy does exist, but existence has a far greater vitality than he supposes. People do have a natural defense. He does not need to watch his thoughts that (underlined) closely.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第405节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "405", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0197", "zh": "你是你自己的内我，这是真的。你给自己设下了自己的难题，但生命力并不全属于你。你已决定用那赐予你、流经你的活力与生命去做某些事，但你无权了结任何一个人格。那些你本可帮助的人，你使他们一无所得；你否拒了那本是你天性应享之权的狂喜。", "en": "You are your own inner self, it is true. You have set your own problems, but the life force is not entirely yours. You have decided to do certain things with the vitality and life that has been given you, that flows through you, but it is not your right to end any given personality. You rob those you could have helped, and you deny the ecstasy that is the natural right of your being.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第440节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "440", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0249", "zh": "那是正确的——只不过在你现在涉及的生活里，你并没有贯注在你活力的全部潜能上。", "en": "That is correct — except that in the life in which you are now involved, you are not focusing upon the full potential of your vitality.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第558节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "558", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0275", "zh": "可是，每个读者，应该多少以一种对他来说很新的方式感觉到了自己的活力，而发现扩展之路在内打开，那些路是他先前没觉察到的。这本书的本质、其创造与传述方法的本身，就应清楚地指出这个事实，即人类人格有远比一般归之于它的多得多的能力。到现在你应了解并不是所有的人格都肉体化了。如这本书就是由一个不具肉体的人格所构思所写，然后再具体化，因此你们每个人都能通达比那些通常被接受的还要更大的能力与通讯方式。", "en": "Each reader, however, should in one way or another sense his own vitality in a way quite new to him, and find avenues of expansion opening within himself of which he was earlier unaware. The very nature of this book, the method of its creation and delivery, in themselves should clearly point out the fact that human personality has far more abilities than those usually ascribed to it. By now you should understand that all personalities are not physically materialized. As this book was conceived and written by a nonphysical personality, and then made physical, so do each of you have access to greater abilities and methods of communication than those usually accepted.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第591节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "591", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0310", "zh": "奥古斯都二被一种有力感充满，因为他认为力量是错的，而把它与他认为的正常自己分开。然而奥古斯都知道，身体需要他拒绝给予它的那股活力。因而奥古斯都二出场了，带着他自己对不同凡响的力量活力和优越感的伟大意念——（较大声而带笑地：）我在把我的两位奥古斯都保持得泾渭分明，我希望你也是的。", "en": "Augustus Two was filled with a sense of power — because Augustus considered power wrong and set it aside from what he thought of as his normal self. Yet Augustus knew the body needed the vitality that he had denied it. Therefore enter Augustus Two with his great ideas of extraordinary power, vigor and superiority — (louder and smiling:) I am keeping my Augustuses straight. I hope you are too.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第633节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "633", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "疗愈的底牌：身体自己就是活力库", "note": "AI总结：内在的生命力和内我有它们自己的疗愈能力，问题只是这些能力很少被利用、被重视。要健康或活力，正确的自我认识少不了：先发现你潜意识里对自己的看法——好意象就以此建立，坏意象就只当它是潜意识的意见而非事实。一切疗愈发生的原因只有一个基本事实：物质是由那些赋予它生机、活力的内在特质形成的，物质的结构随期待而来，而物质随时能被改变。你的身体有一个充满能量与活力的整体身体意识，自动改正任何不平衡——肌肉相信你对它们说的话，身体其他部分也一样。所以那个感觉健康、有活力、有弹性的概括性满足状态，是由众多明确反应带来的；放任不管，身体能对抗任何疾病，却挡不住你对疾病的夸张恐惧——而整套医学系统制造的病跟治好的病一样多，唯独身体的活力和自然防御从没被强调。真正懂行的医生会去确定心灵的模式，他本人就理解灵性活力与身体健康之间的动力学。判断：疗愈不是加东西，是把活力本来就在这件事当真。", "src": "第 73、340、609、624、703、704、804、805、933 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 73 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 340 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 609 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 624 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 703 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 704 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 804 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 805 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 933 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0074", "zh": "以同样的方式，其他的建构也受到影响。的确，成为物质的东西必须被当作物质来处理，内在的生命力和内我有它们自己的疗愈能力。问题是，这些能力很少被利用、被重视。", "en": "In the same manner, other constructions are affected. It is true that what becomes matter must be dealt with as matter, and yet the inner vitality and the inner self have their own ability to heal. The trouble is, these abilities are little utilized and seldom appreciated.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第73节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "73", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0154", "zh": "若想拥有健康或活力，绝对少不了正确的自我认识，任何情况下都是如此。认识自我的真相，意味着必须先在潜意识上发现你对自己的看法。如果这是好的意象，就以此为基准而建立吧，如果是不好的意象，就只要当作是潜意识的意见，而不是确定的事实。", "en": "True self -knowledge is indispensable for health or vitality, and this means in every instance. The recognition of the truth about the self means that you must first discover what you think about yourself subconsciously. If this is a good image, build upon it. If it is a poor one, recognize it as simply the opinion of the subconscious and not as a definite truth.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第340节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "340", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0292", "zh": "希望这本书避免像许多励志书籍中过度乐观的弊病，而激起读者内心一种热切的渴望，想要一探“实相”的特性，即使只为解决他自己的问题。我所要告诉你们的那些方法绝对可行、绝对实际，而且也全都在每一个人的能力可及范围之内，只要你真正关切那些生而为人就必然会有的困难。 书里面将会反复阐明一个事实，那就是所有的疗愈之所以能够发生，乃是因为当事人已经接纳了一个基本的“事实”。这个“事实”是：其一，物质是由那些赋予它生机、活力的“内在特质”所形成的。其二，物质的结构随“期待”而来。其三，“物质”随时都能被改变，改变之道在于唤起所有意识之内与生俱来的创造能力。", "en": "(Still in trance, Jane took a long pause at 10:37. Her eyes closed, she sat rocking back and forth with one foot upon the edge of the coffee table.)", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第609节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "609", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0306", "zh": "这些全是相当实际的声明。你的身体有一个充满了能量与活力的整体身体意识，它自动地改正任何的不平衡，但你有意识的信念也影响整个身体意识。你告诉你的肌肉它们是怎么样，它们就相信自己是那样。你身体的每一个其他部分也都一样。", "en": "These are quite practical statements. Your body has an overall body consciousness filled with energy and vitality. It automatically rights any imbalances, but your conscious beliefs also affect this body consciousness. Your muscles believe what you tell them about themselves. So does every other portion of your physical body.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第624节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "624", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0342", "zh": "在由细胞到“自我”意识的整个完型里有广大的知识领域——其大半现在都能被“无意识地”得到——以用来维持身体在时空里的完整性。以意识心作为指挥者，大半的这些知识没有理由不能变得正常而自然的被得到。因此，有一个相当有效、有活力、真实而极具创造性的内在实相，以及一个向内的事件之顺序，而你们现在的宇宙与生命是由其浮出的。任何真正的科学家终究必须学习进入实相的那个领域，而所谓客观的手段只有当你在处理所谓客观的效应时才可能有任何的作用——而你们的物理学家正学到即使在架构里，也只有在某些频率之内或在某些条件之下，许多的“事实”才是事实，而留下来给你们的只是能帮助你在你们自己的后院里“可用的事实”，但当你试着冒险到你自己宇宙的社区之外时，这种事实就变成了偏见，而你会发现你预先形成的、本土性的想法在它们的范畴之外并不适用。", "en": "Your medical technology may help you “conquer” one disease after another — some in fact caused by that same technology — and you will feel very efficient as you do heart transplants, as you fight one virus after another. But all of this will do nothing except to allow people to die, perhaps, of other diseases still “unconquered.” People will die when they are ready to, following inner dictates and dynamics. A person ready to die will, despite any medication. (Emphatically:) A person who wants to live will seize upon the tiniest hope, and respond. The dynamics of health have nothing to do with inoculations. They reside in the consciousness of each being. In your terms they are regulated by emotions, desires, and thoughts. A true doctor cannot be scientifically objective. He cannot divorce himself from the reality of his patient. Instead, usually, the doctor’s words and very methods literally separate the patient from himself or herself. The malady is seen almost as a thing apart from the patient’s person — but thrust upon it — over which the patient has little control.3 The condition is analyzed, the blood is sampled. It becomes “a blood sample” to the doctor. The patient may silently shout out, “That is not just a blood sample — it is my blood you are taking.” But he [or she] is discouraged from identifying with the blood of his physical being, so that even his own blood seems alien.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第703节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "703", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0345", "zh": "他会试着去确定心灵的模式，并且顺着它们，他会鼓励病人去调准到那内在神谕，以确定病人自己在肉体生命里的目的，并且加强他灵性的力量。完全的医生会是一个人，他有超级的健康，而因此他本身了解那在灵性的活力与身体的健康之间运作的特殊动力学。（热切的：）那会是他的专长。", "en": "He would try to ascertain the patterns of the psyche, and follow them. He would encourage the patient to tune into the private oracle in order to ascertain his or her own purposes in physical life, and to reinforce spiritual strength. The complete physician would be an individual, (male or female), who was in superb health, and therefore understood himself the particular dynamics that operate between spiritual vitality and physical well-being. (Intently:) That would be his specialty.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第704节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "704", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0390", "zh": "觉得自己健康，有活力与有弹性的整个感受，是一种概括性的满足状况——可是却是由众多明确反应所带来的。任由身体做主的话，它能保护自己而对抗任何的疾病。但是，身体无法适当防御对疾病的夸张的普遍性恐惧。身体必须反映你自己的感受与评估。现在，通常而言，你们整个的医学系统真的制造出与被它医好的同样多的疾病——因为你无时无刻不被各式各样疾病的症候所追捕，而充满了对疾病的恐惧，被身体好像有的患病倾向所击倒——而身体的生命力或自然的防御却完全没有受到强调。", "en": "The overall sense of health, vitality, and resiliency is a generalized condition of contentment — brought about, however, by multitudinous specific responses. Left alone, the body can defend itself against any disease, but it cannot defend itself appropriately against an exaggerated general fear of disease on the individual’s part. It must mirror your own feelings and assessments. Usually, now, your entire medical systems literally generate as much disease as is cured — for you are everywhere hounded by the symptoms of various diseases, and filled with the fear of disease, overwhelmed by what seems to be the body’s propensity toward illness — and nowhere is the body’s vitality or natural defense system stressed.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第804节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "804", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0433", "zh": "（“在每个阶段身体都被健康与活力所充满，那些法则并不会改变。鲁柏是安全并且被保护的。那些肯定现在在此是极为重要的。”", "en": "“The body is at each and every stage also filled with health and vitality. Those rules do not change. Ruburt is safe and protected. Those reassurances are highly important here now.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第933节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "933", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0393", "zh": "（“对某些女人而言，不做定期的自我检查将会招致和做检查一样多的恐惧——而因为这些女人的信念是如此严密的追随着官方的医学信念，所以她们做检查要好得多了。在有关健康的这个例子以及所有的例子里，每个女人应该估量所有的证据，检查她的信念而她做她自己的决定。”", "en": "“With some women, not conducting regular self-examinations would rouse as many fears as doing them — and since those women’s beliefs follow official medical ones so strictly, they’re much better off with the examinations. In this and all instances regarding health, each woman should weigh all the evidence, examine her beliefs, and make her own decisions.” I remind the reader that after break ended at 11:35 in the last session (the 804th in Chapter 1), Seth had this to say: “Left alone, the body can defend itself against any disease, but it cannot defend itself appropriately against an exaggerated general fear of disease on the individual’s part. It must mirror your own feelings and assessments. Usually, now, your entire medical systems literally generate as much disease as is cured — for you are everywhere hounded by the symptoms of various diseases, and filled with the fear of disease, overwhelmed by what seems to be the body’s propensity toward illness — and nowhere is the body’s vitality or natural defense system stressed.”", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第805节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": "罗的编注", "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "805", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "婴儿、老人与百岁部落：活力的自然刻度", "note": "AI总结：活力有它的自然基线。婴儿不是生下来就怕环境——他们沉浸在幸福、生命力和生气蓬勃的感觉里，理所当然地认为需求会被满足、宇宙对他们有好感；这种态度天生就在身体的每个原子、细胞和器官里，触发所有促进成长与完成的反应。那是一种天生的生物上的信心——勇气与活力、生物上的乐观；只有当乐观被严重干预，身体机制才会出问题。年龄这一栏上，赛斯的说法很硬：单单年纪本身，从不会导致任何身体灵活度、心智能力或欲望的减退；死亡的时间与方式基本由每个个人决定。有些背负年龄负面信念的老人，在求生的刺激下反而发现了自己伟大的活力。世界某些地区与信念隔绝的人们活过百岁、强壮有活力——因为他们活在自己了解并与之和谐的世界里。健康也不是从蓬勃到萎靡的一条线下坡：与健康相关的阶段几乎无穷多，只是你们的社会只识别、定义了那些健康缺席的阶段。判断：衰老是信念的账单，不是活力的余额。", "src": "第 2、3、652、665、770、902、914 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 2 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 3 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 652 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 665 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 770 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 902 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 914 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0320", "zh": "如果一个年轻人相信“性”是好的，但老年是不好的。那么他就会发现不可能把活力充沛的性生活当做一个较老的人经验的一部分。在梦境中，同属这个年轻人的小孩与老人可能同时存在，而使得这个人对于他生物性一生的全部范围相当觉知。", "en": "If a young adult believes that sex is good but old age is bad, then he or she will find it impossible to consider exuberant sexuality as a portion of an older person’s experience. In the dream state the child and the old man or woman can exist simultaneously, and the individual is made quite aware of the full range of creaturehood.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第652节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "652", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0329", "zh": "有些老人背负了对年龄的负面信念，而他们在求生的刺激之下，发现了自己伟大的活力及更进一步的目的。还有一些曾因“财物是极端的重要”这个信念而盲目迷失的人，发现他们自己一无所有。他们悟到私有财物的相对不重要，而在自己内心感觉到自少年以来未曾体验的“自由的蠢动”。", "en": "There were old people, laden with negative beliefs about age, who discovered great vitality and further purpose under the stimuli of survival. There were people blinded and lost by a belief in the supreme importance of things, who found themselves with nothing left. They realized the relative unimportance of belongings, and felt within themselves the stirring of a freedom they had not experienced since youth.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第665节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "665", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0372", "zh": "在人口过剩的时代，这种机制大概是不被希冀的，但它是人类现今被搁置的一部分，代表自然的能力。在你们世界的某些地区，孤立的人们活过了百岁的年纪，强壮而有活力，因为他们没被你们的信念所触及，也因为他们与他们所知并了解的世界是和谐共存的。于是，当一个小团体企图维持他自己的生物性姿态时，这种第二思春期偶尔发生，并且因而生下孩子。", "en": "In times of overpopulation, this mechanism is hardly desirable, but it is a part of the species held in abeyance now, representing nature’s capabilities. In some areas of your world, isolated peoples live on past a hundred years, vital and strong, because they are untouched by your beliefs, and because they live in sympathy and accord with the world as they know and understand it. Occasionally such second puberties happen then, with resulting childbirth, as a small group attempts to maintain its own biological stance.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第770节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "770", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0420", "zh": "再次的，在我们谈到受苦的资料里（比如见第八九五节），我提到疾病有其目的——在你们的社会里它有一个挽回面子的性质——所以，在此我谈到的是身体自己的能力。就那方面来说，感官不会退化，单单是年纪本身不会导致任何身体灵活度、或心智能力、或欲望的任何减退。死亡必然会降临到每个活着的人，然而，时间与方式基本上是看每个个人而有所不同的。在任何年纪，有意义的工作都是重要的。你无法以嗜好来令老年人满足，正如你也不能以嗜好令年轻人满足一样。但有意义的工作意味着也具有游戏的活力的工作，而就是那游戏在其本身内含着一种治疗及创造性的伟大特质。", "en": "Again, in our material on suffering (see the 895th session, for instance), I mentioned that illness serves purposes—that it has a face-saving quality in your society—so here I am speaking of the body’s own abilities. In that light, the senses do not fade. Age alone never brought about any loss of physical agility, or of mental ability, or of desire. Death must come to every living person, yet the time and the means are basically up to each individual. Meaningful work is important at any age. You cannot content the aged entirely with hobbies any more than you can the young, but meaningful work means work that also has the exuberance of play, and it is that playful quality that contains within itself great propensities of a healing and creative nature.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第902节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "902", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0427", "zh": "那信念在基因系统的确切作用上是不可或缺的，它是个人健康以及任何一个“族类”整体活力的一个先决条件。你们最伟大的成就正是那些文明所造就的，那时的人对于生命大体而言的意义，以及个人在生命架构里的意义有最大的信心。", "en": "It is vital for the proper workings of genetic systems. It is a prerequisite for individual health and for the overall vitality of any given “stock.” Your greatest achievements have been produced by civilizations during those times when man had the greatest faith in the meaningfulness of life in general, and in the meaningfulness of the individual within life’s framework.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第914节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "914", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0452", "zh": "那些态度都与生俱来地在身体最小的精微部分里——每个原子、细胞和器官的一部分，而它们用来激发所有会促进成长与完成的身体反应。婴儿并非生下来就害怕它们的环境，或其它生物的。反之，它们沉浸在幸福、生命力和生气蓬勃的感觉里。它们视为理所当然，需求将被满足，而宇宙是对它们很有好感的。它们觉得是其环境的一部分。", "en": "Those attitudes are inbred in the smallest microscopic portions of the body — a part of each atom and cell and organ, and they serve to trigger all of the body’s responses that promote growth and fulfillment. Infants are not born with an inbred fear of their environment, or of other creatures. They are instead immersed in feelings of well-being, vitality, and exuberance. They take it for granted that their needs will be met, and that the universe is well-disposed toward them. They feel a part of their environment.", "source": "健康之道 · 第2节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "2", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0457", "zh": "在所有这种例子里，都有一种天生的生物上的信心，那种勇气与活力，那种生物上的乐观。它在人类里也一样的作用，激发必要的身体上的反应。只有当那乐观被严重地干预时，肉体的机制才会出问题。不过，即使那时，所有的生物都是被那与生俱有的礼物所护持的，那内在的安全感，不仅推动生物朝向生命，也还安全地指挥它们历经肉体生命并通过死亡的门户。", "en": "In all such cases there is an inbred biological faith, that courage and vitality, that biological optimism. It acts the same in people, triggering the necessary bodily responses. Only when that optimism is severely tampered with do the physical mechanisms falter. Even then, however, all creatures are sustained by that innate gift, that inner sense of security that not only propels creatures toward life, but safely conducts them past physical life and past death’s doorway.", "source": "健康之道 · 第2节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "2", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0463", "zh": "有不可胜数的健康阶段，从高亢、纯粹、精力充沛的蓬勃生气（停顿良久）到越来越少的活力的减少及不适。在那句话里，删掉“越来越少的”。事实上，几乎有数不清的、与健康相关的阶段。你可以借由将这每个阶段加以编号及定义，而发明一个完全不同的看健康的方法。当然，反之，你们的社会已选择、识别及界定，所有那些对健康不利的阶段——可被认出的阶段，因为到某个程度健康缺席了。", "en": "There are innumerable stages of health, from high, sheer, energetic exuberance (long pause) to dwindling lethargy and discomfort. In that sentence, scratch out “dwindling.” There are, in fact, an almost infinite number of stages connected with the state of health. You could invent a completely different way of regarding human health by numbering and defining each of those stages. Instead, of course, your society has chosen to recognize and define all of those stages that are detrimental to health — stages that are recognizable because of health’s absence to one degree or another.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "把活力找回来：睡眠、游戏、兴趣与肯定语", "note": "AI总结：具体怎么充能，赛斯给过一整包方法。自我暗示的着重点必须是健康、朝气、弹性、力量和生命力，而不是症状——别把注意力钉在症状上；人格确实能靠给自己暗示提神的梦来恢复活力，而且经常自动这样做。睡眠里最受保护的区域具有最强的恢复活力特性，多而短的睡眠让身心活动更新更稳，你所知的意识也会变得更有弹性、更有活力。兴趣是另一条路：他需要其他兴趣来使自己恢复活力——重拾绘画、开心地做瑜伽、不必总那么正经八百，这些给内我自由的空间。当自发性被容许并回归时，改善本身就是活力增强与释放的征兆。作为自然生物，你内里有一种自然的存在状态，那是和平、活力与了解的常备库藏。也别忘了玩：有意义的工作是带着游戏的活力的工作，而游戏本身就含着治疗与创造的特质。最后，接受直觉、感受、梦和神奇的希望是个人性的重要特质而非附属品，那些被闲置的特性会毫不费力地把丰富成就和活力加进你的生命。判断：活力不用「补」，用「放」——把闸门和羞耻拿掉，它自己回来。", "src": "第 1、6、186、323、325、400、424、532、569、799 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 1 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 6 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 186 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 323 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 325 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 400 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 424 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 532 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 569 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 799 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0125", "zh": "它很容易受暗示影响。鲁伯今晚打趣地说，他会暗示自己做个提神的梦，这真的是绝佳的暗示。人格的确能以这种方式让自我恢复活力，而且经常自动这样做。", "en": "It is very susceptible to suggestion. Ruburt's jesting remark this evening that he would suggest refreshing dreams was actually an excellent one. The personality can indeed refresh itself in such a manner, and often does automatically.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第186节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "186", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0148", "zh": "在其他方向上的兴趣强度，比时间重要多了。我们不想要把注意力集中在症状上。在所有的催眠课上以及所有的自我暗示期间，的确应该强调健康、朝气、弹性、力量和生命力。今天我跟鲁柏提起这件事，但他认为这个主意是他自己的。", "en": "The intensity of interest in other directions is much more important than time. We do not want intense concentration upon the symptoms. In all hypnotic sessions and in all periods of self suggestion, emphasis should indeed be upon health, exuberance, flexibility, strength and vitality. I mentioned this to Ruburt today, but he thought the idea his own.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第323节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "323", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0151", "zh": "在任何情况下，暗示都必须强调健康和活力。比方说，专注在一只手上，看看某一个暗示是否渗透入里，几乎没什么好处。鲁柏现在处于释放相当多能量的阶段，现在他必须把它用在建设性的活动上，而不是症状。", "en": "In all cases emphasis on suggestions must be upon health and vitality. To concentrate upon a hand for example to see whether or not a suggestion has taken hold, is hardly beneficial. Ruburt is now at the stage where he has freed considerable energy, and this must now be utilized in constructive activity, and not to reinforce symptoms. It will be highly advantageous now for him to renew projection attempts. 4904105-568960f", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第325节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "325", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0172", "zh": "不仅如此，他还需要其他兴趣来使自己恢复活力。我过去曾建议他恢复绘画，瑜伽不错，对他来说非常好，应该开心地做，他不必一直都那么正经八百。这几点听起来简单易懂，但是要去遵循，这些会给内我自由的空间。他又在鞭策自己，虽然现在是为了更好的目标而这样做。（微笑）", "en": "Not only this, but he needs other interests to refresh him. I have in the past suggested he resume painting. The yoga is good, excellent for him. It should be done joyfully. He need not always be so serious. These points sound obvious, but they should be followed. This gives the inner self freedom. He has been hammering again, though now he hammers with a better purpose. (Smile.)", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第400节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "400", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0187", "zh": "其他一些切身方面的改善也已显现，它们是活力增强与释放的征兆，因为自发性得到容许，并且回归了。整个状况都更好了。这个改变是好的。", "en": "Other intimate improvements have shown themselves, and they are symptoms of increased vitality and release, as spontaneity is allowed for, and returns. The whole condition is better. The change was good.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第424节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "424", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0244", "zh": "较多、较短的睡眠，结果使有意识的贯注达到更高的顶峰，并且身心活动都有更稳定的更新。在“自己”的各区域或各层面间也比较没有那么确定的分界。结果会造成精力更经济的利用，和养分更有效的利用。你所知道的意识也会变得更有弹性、更有活力。", "en": "As a result of more frequent, briefer sleep periods, there would also be higher peaks of conscious focus, and a more steady renewal of both physical and psychic activity. There would not be such a definite division between the various areas or levels of the self. A more economical use of energy would result, and also a more effective use of nutrients. Consciousness as you know it would also become more flexible and mobile.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第532节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "532", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0260", "zh": "其实这在每晚的睡眠中都会发生，它涉及了两个活动区域，一个非常被动，而一个则极端主动。在某个状况下意识的这部分是被动的，在接受情报。而在下一阶段当它透过行动来参与时，它是主动的——那时它透过参与和实例很鲜明的感知到所给予它的观念。这是睡眠里最受保护最隐密的区域，在这里也最具有恢复活力的特性，而“说法者”就是在这一个阶段里扮演教师与向导。", "en": "Now this happens in every night’s sleep. Two areas of activity are involved, one very passive and one acutely active. In one state this portion of consciousness is passive, receiving information. In the next stage it is active as it takes part through action — the concepts given it are then vividly perceived through participation and examples. This is the most protected area of sleep. The rejuvenating characteristics enter in here, and it is during this period that the Speakers act as teachers and guides.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第569节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "569", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0381", "zh": "因为你们是自然的生物，在你们内有一种自然的存在状态。那种状态可以是和平、活力和了解的一个永在的库藏。", "en": "Because you are natural creatures, within you there is a natural state of being. That state can be an ever-present reservoir of peace, vitality, and understanding.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第799节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "799", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0437", "zh": "纵然如此，男人和女人仍然借由重新发现更大意义的身分——那是接受直觉和感受、梦和神奇的希望为「个人性」之重要特性，而非附属物的一种身分感——而找到他们许多问题的答案。当我告诉你，要记住你自己的自然人时，那么我就是真的想要提醒你，别光只与你的知性认同，而应去扩大你身分的范围。然后自然而然地，那些其它的、往往被唾弃的特性，便开始毫不费力地将它们的丰富成就和活力，增加到你的生命里。", "en": "Despite all of that, men and women still find the solutions to many of their problems by rediscovering the larger sense of identity1 — a sense of identity that accepts the intuitions and the feelings, the dreams and the magic hopes as vital characteristics, not adjuncts, of personhood. When I tell you to remember your own natural persons, I do then want to remind you not to identify with your intellects alone, but to enlarge your scopes of identity. Automatically those other, often-shunted-aside characteristics begin to add their richness, fulfillment, and vitality to your lives effortlessly.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第6节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "6", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0441", "zh": "身体意识，在其本身，是充满了活力、生气及创造性的。", "en": "The body consciousness, on its own, is filled with exuberance, vitality, and creativity.", "source": "健康之道 · 第1节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "1", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "活力往外流：思想、家庭与群体事件", "note": "AI总结：活力不只在你皮肤之内。你不停向外发出心电感应式的思想：一个家庭若把注意力放在生机、力量与创造性的念头上，就能不断加强它的喜悦与自发性；反过来强化怨恨与怀疑，就等于让一半的能量白白溜走。思想的活力很少有人认真掂量——你说思想阻止不了战争，可你认为是什么开动的战争？个人与群体的关系也一样：卷入主义的人若坚持自己的个人性而非屈居于主义之下，就把那份活力加给了他们相信的事业——他们是被热情与活力、好奇与爱驱动，而不是被恐惧驱动。有人靠一连串外部危机来让自己内在的特质保持鲜活；甚至流行文化里的神仙教母，也是架构二的人格化——当内我这样回应时，平凡的环境会突然充满一种新的活力。往大处说，死亡在生物上是必要的，不只是为了个人，也是为确保族类生生不息的活力；而像人质危机这样的群体事件，则是物质化了的群体的梦，意在把信念冲突戏剧化。判断：群体议题在赛斯这儿也是活力账——谁在给系统充电，谁在放电。", "src": "第 617、800、801、824、835、848、857、891 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 617 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 800 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 801 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 824 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 835 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 848 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 857 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 891 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0301", "zh": "如我以前提到的（在第六一六节里），你也不停地放出自己的心电感应思想。别人也就根据他们自己对实相的意念而作出反应。借着把注意力集中在生机、力量与创造性的念头上，一个家庭能不断地加强它的喜悦（较大声地）、欢乐和自发性；或者借着加强怨恨、愤怒、怀疑与失败的想法，（较低沉地）也可以让它一半的能量白白溜走。", "en": "As I mentioned earlier (in the 616th session), you are also sending your own telepathic thoughts outward. Others will react to those according to their own ideas of reality. A family can constantly reinforce its joy (louder), gaiety, and spontaneity by concentrating on ideas of vitality, strength and creativity; or it can let half of its energy slip away (deeper) by reinforcing resentments, angers and thoughts of doubt and failure.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第617节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "617", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0384", "zh": "思想的力量、活力和效力很少被考虑。你也许会说，思想不能阻止一场战争，然而，你认为是什么开始了这样的战争？有史以来，被蹂躏者常常变得握有实力，利用暴力反叛他们的压制者；却没从那经验学到多少，他们转而变成新的菁英，新的掌权者。他们的实质状况可能完全改变了。现在政府的机构、财富成了他们的。看起来好像引起叛乱的情况已没了。但是他们却在报复中出击，形成一个新的被蹂躏的阶级，而他们必会在轮到他们的时候起而报复。", "en": "The strength, vitality, and effectiveness of thought is seldom considered. Thought, you may say, will not stop a war — yet what do you think started such a war? Throughout history the downtrodden have often risen into power, using force, rebelling against their oppressors; and yet, learning little from that experience, they turn and become the new elite, the new power-holders. Their physical conditions may be completely changed. Now theirs, the offices of government, the wealth. Gone are the conditions that, it would seem, caused the uprising. Yet in retaliation they strike out, forming a new class of downtrodden who must in their turn rise and retaliate.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第800节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "800", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0387", "zh": "死亡在生物上是必要的，不只是对个人而言，而且也是要确保人类生生不息的活力。死亡是一种心灵与心理上的必然，因为过了一阵子，灵魂充溢的、不断更新的能量不再能被转译到肉体里去了。", "en": "We have begun Part 1, to be called: “The Events of ‘Nature.’ Epidemics and Natural Disasters.”", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第801节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "801", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0396", "zh": "这故事一直对儿童有吸引力，因为他们认出在其后的合理性。那个神仙教母是“架构二”个人化了里的成分之一个具有创造性的人格化——因而，是“内我”的一个人格化，起来帮助肉身的自己而回应其愿望，甚至当这肉身自己的意图看来也许并不切合正常人生的实际架构时。当内我以这样一种方式反应，甚至那平凡、普通、看来无害的环境就突然变得充满了一种新的活力，而好像对所涉及的那个人“有利”了。如果你正在看这本书，你就已经老到不会清楚记得你幼年时经常不断的幻想了。可是，儿童们自动的知道得十分清楚，他们在那些“对他们发生的”事件之创造上有很强烈的参与，而后那些事再仿佛对他们发生。", "en": "The tale has always appealed to children because they recognize the validity behind it.2 The fairy godmother is a creative personification of the personalized elements in Framework 2 — a personification therefore of the inner ego, that rises to the aid of the mortal self to grant its desires, even when the intents of the mortal self may not seem to fit into the practical framework of normal life. When the inner ego responds in such a fashion, even the commonplace, ordinary, seemingly innocuous circumstances suddenly become charged with a new vitality, and appear to “work for” the individual involved. If you are reading this book you are already too old to clearly remember the constant fantasies of your early childhood. Children however know quite well, automatically, that they have a strong hand in the creation of the events that then seem to happen to them.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第824节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "824", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0399", "zh": "所以你无法信任自己的直觉。你认为你在人生中的目的必然是作别的东西或别的人，而非作你自己。在这样一种情形里，许多人寻求主义，而希望把那主义的目的与他们自己未被认出的目的合在一起。会有许多伟大的人卷入主义里，而把他们的精力、资源与支持都给了那些主义。不过，那些人承认他们自己存在的重要性，而把那份活力加到他们相信的主义上。他们不把他们的个人性屈居于主义之下，却反而坚持他们的个人性而变得更是他们自己。他们扩展了眼界，向前推进而超越了因袭的精神景观——被热情和活力、好奇与爱，而非恐惧所驱策（非常强调的说以上所有的话）。", "en": "Therefore, you cannot trust your own intuitions. You think that your purpose in life must be to be something else, or someone else, than you are. In such a situation many people seek out causes, and hope to merge the purposes of the cause with their own unrecognized one. There have been many great men and women involved in causes, to which they gave their energies, resources, and support. Those people, however, recognized the importance of their own beings, and added that vitality to causes in which they believed. They did not submerge their individuality to causes. Instead, they asserted their individuality, and became more themselves. They extended their horizons, pushed beyond the conventional mental landscapes — driven by zest and vitality, by curiosity and love, and not by fear (all of the above with much emphasis).", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第835节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "835", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0402", "zh": "他们生活中所有事件之发生，都多少被这灾难的可能性加上标点或加料。他们觉得无论何时都可能会被促使去面对最大的挑战、去依赖他们最强的应变能力、他们最大的耐力，并且面对一个耐力的考验。他们用——或他们常用——这样一种心理与物理的背景来在他们自己内维持住那些特质的活力，因为他们是那种喜欢感受到与一个挑战对抗的人。通常，这种可能性的存在及其接受，的确提供了一种外在的危机状况，那在个人与群体来说象征了独立与内心的危机。那个危机在外在情况被面对，而当人们在处理那个情况时，他们象征性的处理了他们自己的内在危机。以一种说法，那些人信任这种外在的对抗，甚至为这种目的，仰赖一连串有种种不同严重程度的危机（热切的）而利用一辈子。", "en": "To one extent or another, all of the events of their lives happen punctuated or accented by the possibility of disaster. They feel that at any time they might be caused to face the greatest challenge, to rely upon their strongest resources, their greatest forbearance, and faced by a test of endurance. They use — or they often use — such a psychological and physical backdrop to keep those qualities alive within themselves, for they are the kind of people who like to feel pitted against a challenge. Often the existence of probabilities and their acceptance does provide a kind of exterior crisis situation that individually and en masse is a symbol of independence and inner crisis. The crisis is met in the exterior situation, and as the people deal with that situation they symbolically deal with their own inner crises. In a way (underlined) those people trust such exterior confrontations, and even count upon a series of them (intently), of varying degrees of severity, that can be used throughout a lifetime for such purposes.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第848节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "848", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0405", "zh": "一个民主制度是一种极为有趣的政府形式，它是非常重要的，因为它要求这么多的个人意识，而且因为它主要必须寄托在对个人力量的信念上。在你们的国家里，那个信念流连了这么久，而且在面对由科学与宗教所持的相当相反的公认信念时，它还能以如此的活力运作，这实在是对那个信念的一种赞美。", "en": "A democracy is a highly interesting form of government, highly significant because it demands so much of individual consciousness, and because it must rest primarily upon a belief in the powers of the individual. It is a tribute to that belief that it has lingered in your country, and operated with such vitality in the face of quite opposing beliefs officially held by both science and religion.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第857节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "857", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0411", "zh": "像整个的美国人质事件（在伊朗），任意一个实质事件成为一个焦点，吸引了它所有的可能版本和结果。人质的情况（现在已是第53天）是个物质化了的群体的梦，它意在将其重要性与活力显示在实相的政治和宗教舞台上，意在将信念的冲突戏剧化，并把那冲突向外投射到众所周知的领域。在人类行为最基本的层面，每个涉及的人都有意识或无意识的自愿参与，当然，1980年即刻被那事件先罩上了阴影。这世界将拿它怎么办？", "en": "Like the entire American hostage affair (in Iran), any physical event serves as a focus that attracts all of its probable versions and outcomes. The hostage situation (now in day 53) is a materialized mass dream, meant to be important and vital on political and religious platforms of reality, meant to dramatize a conflict of beliefs, and to project that conflict outward into the realm of public knowledge. Everyone involved was consciously and unconsciously a willing participant at the most basic levels of human behavior, and it is of course no coincidence that 1980 is immediately foreshadowed by that event. What will the world do with it?", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第891节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "891", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "一个「死人」的活力课：赛斯的现身说法", "note": "AI总结：最能说明活力本质的，是赛斯自己的做派。他在ESP班上冲着学员喊：按你们的说法我是死了！那你们怎么反倒了无生气？为什么非得由我来告诉你们什么是生命力？——一个「灰色的鬼魂」比满屋子活人更有生命力，这本身就是教材。他给学生的健康建议也落在活力上：心存安宁与生命力的念头、向人祝好，你就在帮助疗愈——灵性疗愈的力量你本来就在用。他对珍和罗说，他关心的是你们整体的灵性活力，而不是你早餐吃了什么；活力被他放在所有关切的第一位。他也拿它谈选择：胆量必须用，否则可能摧毁你生命力的根基，别把能量耗费在无所事事的嗜好上，但要确定你是在为善塑造你的公司。往深处走，连临终都是活力的事：到了那个时候，人自己知道，心灵的伟大活力不再想被一个受苦的身体囚禁。而在或然系统里，罗父亲最大的活力是在那个发明家的实相里——活力在哪个实相绽放，是每个自己的选择。判断：活力不是「活着」的副词，它就是赛斯想让你认领的那个主词。", "src": "第 439、483、493、501、578、615、661、679、680 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 439 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 483 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 493 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 501 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 578 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 615 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 661 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 679 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 680 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-030-e0192", "zh": "你不能再把你的胆量花费在海盗船上了。（幽默地。）但你必须用它，否则它可能摧毁你生命力的根基。不要把能量耗费在无所事事的嗜好追求上。它们骗不了你。但要确定：当你试着把活力吹进你的公司、去塑造它时，你是为了善而塑造它。你有一个机会——用上它。", "en": "You cannot use your daring in pirate ships any longer. (Humorous.) But use it you must or it could destroy the foundations of your vitality. Do not spend your energy in idle hobby pursuits. They do not fool you. But make sure that when you try to breathe vitality into your company, and form it, that you form it for the good. You have an opportunity—use it.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第439节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "439", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0218", "zh": "你们已有灵性疗愈的力量。你们想知道怎样使用它。其实无论你们知不知道，你们都在使用它。当你们心存安宁与生命力的念头，当你们向人祝好，你们就在帮助疗愈他。", "en": "You already have the power of spiritual healing. You want to know how to use it. Now you use it whether or not you know that you do. When you think thoughts of peace and vitality, and when you wish a man well, then you help heal him.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第483节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "483", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0223", "zh": "按你们的说法，我是死了！（非常大声。）那你们又怎会反倒了无生气？为什么非得由我来告诉你们什么是生命力……按你们的说法，我不过是一个灰色的鬼魂，在夜的幽暗里飘忽来去……是一张从二楼窗外向内窥探的脸（说的是[SW]近日被她窗口出现的一张脸吓着了那件事），迎来的一切回应不过一声惊骇的叹息。我去拜访我的朋友，他们几乎当场晕过去。（[SW]致了歉。）", "en": "Now, in your terms. I am dead! (Very loud.) How can you then be less lively? Why is it that I must tell you what vitality is... when, in your terms, I am a gray ghost that flits through the darkness of the night... a face that peers through second-story windows (in reference to SW's being frightened by a face that appeared at her window recently) and meets with no response but a sigh of horror. I visit my friends and they nearly faint. (SW apologized.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第493节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "493", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0228", "zh": "我还要你们大家知道，这不是录音，我也没有事先备好课程。我确实是来赴一场面对面的相遇的，来问候我们的客人——而你们也得承认，就一位像我这样年长的绅士而言，我身上还剩着几分活力呢。（此处声音极洪亮。）", "en": "And I want you all to know that this is no recording and I have not prepared my lesson ahead of time. I have indeed come for a personal encounter, and to greet our guests and you must admit that for a gentleman as old as I there is some vitality left in me yet. (Very loud in here.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第501节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "501", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0265", "zh": "因此，我大体觉察你们的情形。如果任何事扰乱了鲁柏，他会自动地发给我关于它的讯息。在我提到过的限制内，我对你们生活中的未来事件是知道的（停顿）。我对你整个灵魂的活力比对你早餐吃了什么要关心多了。", "en": "(Pause at 11:25.) I am generally aware, therefore, of your condition. If anything upsets Ruburt, he automatically sends me messages about it. I am aware, within the limitations mentioned, of future events in your lives. (Pause.) I am much more concerned with your overall spiritual vitality than I am with what you had for breakfast.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第578节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "578", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0296", "zh": "你的灵魂结合了肉体而存在于肉体中，是为了要经历一个无比丰富的世界，是为了要协力创造一个有色有相的实相。你的灵魂生于肉体中，是为了要丰富感官知觉的神妙领域，是为了要体会能量被造成具体形态时的感受。你在这里是为了要透过身体来享受、来表达、来运用自己。你在这里是要帮助意识的伟大扩展。你出生不是为了替人类的苦痛号哭，而是当你发现不喜欢它们时，透过你内心的喜悦、力量和活力来改变它们，你要做的是尽可能信实而美丽地在你的身体中创造心灵。", "en": "Your spirit joined itself with flesh, and in flesh, to experience a world of incredible richness, to help create a dimension of reality of colors and of form. Your spirit was born in flesh to enrich a marvelous area of sense awareness, to feel energy made into corporeal form. You are here to use, enjoy, and express yourself through the body. You are here to aid in the great expansion of consciousness. You are not here to cry about the miseries of the human condition, but to change them when you find them not to your liking through the joy, strength and vitality that is within you; to create the spirit as faithfully and beautifully as you can in flesh.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第615节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "615", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0324", "zh": "如果，它被它的兄弟所杀，这并不是一种残忍的举动，却是对这个生物已不能没有痛苦地活下去的一种天生了解；这涉及了一个十分自然的“安乐死”，在其中，“病人”也予以默许了。 在你们的社会里，这样的自然死亡是非常困难的，因为你们的权力结构使得这种事几乎无法提倡。然而，没有一个决定要死的人能被医学界救回来。以你们的话来说，在更深的层面，想要存活的正常的渴望，使得一个人迟早必须离开他的身体。当那个时候来到时，这个人就会知道，心灵的伟大活力也不再想被一个受苦的身体囚禁了。", "en": "When and if it is killed by its brothers, this is not an act of cruelty but an innate understanding that the creature can no longer operate physically without agony; a quite natural euthanasia is involved, in which the “patient” also acquiesces. In your society such a natural death is most difficult, and because of the power structures can hardly be promoted. No one who decides upon death is saved from it by the medical profession, however. On deeper levels the quite normal desire for survival requires that the individual leave his or her body, in your terms, at one time or another. When that period arrives the person knows it, and the great vitality of the spirit no longer wants to be encased by a suffering physical body.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第661节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "661", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0334", "zh": "那个孩子享受着很棒的活力与安全的感觉。你的家庭关系一直是很好的，你大半被爱与肯定环绕着。你的双亲很年轻，你母亲那时已生下两个漂亮的男孩；而她以她自己的方式，而且在她自己的架构里，也是个完美主义者——你父亲从来没了解到她这点。", "en": "That child enjoys great feelings of vigor and safety. In your family relationship so far, so good. You were mainly surrounded by love and affirmation. Your parents were young. Your mother had produced two beautiful boys; and she was also a perfectionist in her way, and in her framework — one never understood by your father.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第679节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "679", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-030-e0336", "zh": "你父亲之最大活力是在那发明家的实相里，因此，以你们的话来说，你这个父亲就吃亏了。这并不是说每个人格——不论在那个可能性——没被赋予自由意志及其他等等。在不论那个系统里，每一个都是由一个源头完形能量生出而发展的。", "en": "Your father’s greatest vitality was in the inventor’s reality, and so in your terms this one suffered. This does not mean that each personality, regardless of probabilities, is not endowed with free will, and so forth. Each is born, in whatever system, from a source gestalt energy, and develops.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第680节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "680", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 7}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 7}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 4}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 4}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 4}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 3}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 3}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 8, "quotes": 72, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 1, "only_en": 25}};
